WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.017 --> 00:00:05.880
Speaker 1: Moving on. We've talked a lot about&nbsp;
Republicans. It's now time to talk about some&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.880 --> 00:00:11.040
problems that the Democrats have. And it's&nbsp;
a problem, unfortunately, named Democratic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.040 --> 00:00:17.340
Senator Dianne Feinstein. This week, of course, it&nbsp;
was revealed that Feinstein has missed 60 votes.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.340 --> 00:00:24.480
Her absence from the Senate committee is actually&nbsp;
preventing Biden's judicial nominees from being&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:28.920
confirmed. They can't move out of committee&nbsp;
because they have to have her vote, but she's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.920 --> 00:00:34.320
been out since early March with shingles. She is&nbsp;
now out of the hospital. Of course, she only spent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:41.640
a few days there. She's been recuperating in her&nbsp;
home in California. She's 89 years old. She is not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.640 --> 00:00:48.120
running for reelection. Her term ends at the end&nbsp;
of the year 2024, and it's time for her to resign.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.620 --> 00:00:55.560
That is my personal opinion. I think it's time for&nbsp;
Dianne Feinstein to resign. But I'm not saying she&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.560 --> 00:00:59.700
has to resign because of her health issue. I'm&nbsp;
not saying she has to resign because of her age.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:09.240
My plan my idea is I have a plan. I have no&nbsp;
control over any of this. My idea is she needs to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.240 --> 00:01:15.000
resign for the good of the Democratic Party, not&nbsp;
for the Biden judges thing. But for the House of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:22.920
Representatives. We got three Democrats that are&nbsp;
going to be running in that Senate primary next&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.920 --> 00:01:29.880
year. And because they're running in the Senate&nbsp;
primary, they cannot run for their House seats.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.260 --> 00:01:36.960
So three of those Democrats running, at least&nbsp;
two of them obviously will lose their seats&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.960 --> 00:01:44.040
and will no longer be elected officials here in&nbsp;
the United States. And what terrifies me are the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.040 --> 00:01:51.480
people we could lose. We could lose Katie Porter&nbsp;
and Barbara Lee from the House of Representatives.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.980 --> 00:01:59.340
That thought terrifies me. I love them&nbsp;
both. They are vital voices in that House&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.340 --> 00:02:04.980
of Representatives. We need them there. The&nbsp;
third person running, of course, is Adam Schiff.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.300 --> 00:02:09.960
And I hate to say it, but I think Schiff&nbsp;
is probably the shoo in for this job.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.920 --> 00:02:16.020
I don't want him to be the one to get it. I'd love&nbsp;
to have Katie Porter in the Senate. I'd love to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.020 --> 00:02:20.160
have Barbara Lee in the Senate. But I don't want&nbsp;
it to come at the expense of the other one having&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.160 --> 00:02:25.500
a job as an elected official because they're&nbsp;
both good people. So how do we overcome that?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.940 --> 00:02:33.540
Dianne Feinstein resigns. What happens when she&nbsp;
resigns? While California is one of 37 states&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.540 --> 00:02:38.880
that says if a senator resigns or, you know, is&nbsp;
no longer in office during the rest of their term,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.600 --> 00:02:42.900
the governor gets to a point, their&nbsp;
replacement until the next election.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.820 --> 00:02:50.220
Gavin Newsom. Would be able to appoint&nbsp;
the replacement. That replacement&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.420 --> 00:02:56.160
is the one who would most likely go on&nbsp;
to obviously be the nominee for 2024,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.160 --> 00:03:05.160
which could get rid of the need for the primary.&nbsp;
Which means we wouldn't lose those Democrats from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.160 --> 00:03:10.740
the House. Now, I know that's a weird idea because&nbsp;
it takes away the primary. It may not. I mean,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.740 --> 00:03:13.680
if they still want a primary, they can&nbsp;
still primary. They still have the option.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.700 --> 00:03:21.420
But it kind of solidifies, you know, listen,&nbsp;
here's what we can do. So, Gavin Newsom.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.320 --> 00:03:27.720
Needs to go meet with Dianne Feinstein. They&nbsp;
need to have this talk. They need to work&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.720 --> 00:03:33.660
this out. Feinstein does need to be a part of the&nbsp;
conversation. My God, she has been in office. She&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.660 --> 00:03:38.580
deserves to be part of the conversation. She's&nbsp;
been there for so long. She is an institution.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:39.660 --> 00:03:45.420
But she has also done her service and it's&nbsp;
time to pass that torch. But that torch has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:45.420 --> 00:03:50.160
to be passed in a way that doesn't screw over the&nbsp;
Democratic Party in the House of Representatives.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:50.160 --> 00:03:54.120
And right now, that is exactly what we're headed&nbsp;
towards. Like, that's what's going to happen.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:55.380 --> 00:04:01.980
But we can avoid that if she resigns. And&nbsp;
Gavin Newsom can appoint that replacement.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:03.720 --> 00:04:06.780
So Gavin Newsom could say,&nbsp;
Listen. All right, Katie Porter,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:07.620 --> 00:04:13.920
you're the senator now. Which would mean&nbsp;
obviously, Katie Porter wouldn't lose her seat.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:14.580 --> 00:04:20.640
We could probably avoid a messy primary at&nbsp;
that point. And go from there. He could say,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:20.640 --> 00:04:26.580
Barbara Lee, you're the senator now. That may make&nbsp;
Katie Porter say, okay, look, if she's got it now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:26.580 --> 00:04:30.300
clearly she'll win the primary. I'm going to back&nbsp;
out. I'm going to keep going on my House seat.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:31.620 --> 00:04:36.540
It may not work the way that I'm thinking.&nbsp;
You know, I could be wrong about this.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:36.540 --> 00:04:41.100
This is just my idea, my theory. But I&nbsp;
think it's the best and smartest move.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:42.480 --> 00:04:49.320
Let Feinstein resign on her own terms.&nbsp;
Let her have a say in what happens to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:49.320 --> 00:04:53.400
the seat. I know that's not how politics is&nbsp;
supposed to work. The people get the choice.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:56.220 --> 00:04:58.140
But for the good of the Democratic Party.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:59.760 --> 00:05:04.380
We can't lose those voices for the good of the&nbsp;
country. We can't lose both those voices in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:04.380 --> 00:05:10.860
house. We simply cannot. And this may avoid that&nbsp;
may not be the prettiest scenario, may not be the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:10.860 --> 00:05:15.840
thing that everybody loves to do. But I think&nbsp;
it's the smartest path forward at this point.

